    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1aabab7ae39174b4f22edca47f96a7c321492e7b2ca90bd44861fc6f9cd19804",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Expectation placement creates an information hierarchy and different conditional routes to RH. Jensen sends pNB to gNB, but the paper's pNB route extracts one admissible outcome through Assumption (P), whereas its gNB route controls a deterministic averaged kernel through an admissible Mellin target, summed moments, and coefficient-weighted tails. The examples confirm that these are distinct proof mechanisms: condition (C) is not required by the displayed concentrated-family pNB implication, and correlation effects are left open.",
