    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_8bc574355ab083abc69a8a26e7c3b63ba22c2f3cb0709f8e2193184eaec66dc8",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The survival-function identity E{X/t}=-Pf(t) converts expected random fractional-part kernels into deterministic Muntz transforms. For Z_k=X/k, RH therefore supplies bounded good-kernel approximation coefficients and gNB plus condition (C); in the reverse direction, admissibility, summed moments, and the coefficient-weighted tail condition let a moving-cutoff Mellin argument replace the compact-support tail simplification and exclude zeros. Together these give the stated conditional equivalence for the dilated class.",
