    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_f1046347af85ca7ec131fd2a9901503523bc5c7c095a36e46f8a935fafd72c69",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Assumption (P) gives the same admissible-support event two complementary roles. Combined with pNB and Markov, it overlaps a small-error event and selects one deterministic Nyman-Beurling witness; combined with the deterministic distance bound at the random minimum m_n, it transfers a scale obstruction back to the expected error, yielding D_n^2 bounded below up to constants by 1/(log 2 + E|log m_n|).",
